A-Share Lockup / Insider Context:
- Lockup expiry (限售股解禁) is a major supply-side event — large unlocks can depress prices
- IPO lockups (12-month) and private placement lockups (6-36 months) are the most common types
- Pre-IPO shareholder unlocks (大小非) are the most significant — original shareholders with near-zero cost basis
- Major shareholder reductions (大股东减持) require pre-disclosure; track announced reduction plans
- Insider buying (高管增持) is a strong positive signal, especially clustered buying after significant declines
- Share buybacks (股份回购) are increasingly common and signal management confidence
- Pledge risk (股权质押): check if major shareholders have high pledge ratios — margin call risk in downtrends

